#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Dressed boxes {#dressed-boxes}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Physical noise mechanisms that occur during the execution of quantum "
"circuits are contextual. When applying operations on disjoint sets of qubits"
" simultaneously, the noise profile of the overall operation might differ "
"from the noise profiles of the constituent parts if they were applied in "
"isolation. Similarly, for operations that ideally commute on the same "
"qubits, the noise profile associated with the individual operations might "
"not commute and could be different altogether if the order of the operations"
" changed. Therefore, protocols for suppressing, mitigating, and correcting "
"noise need to know the context in which it arises.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Samplomatic uses box instructions to reason about collections of circuit "
"operations that should be treated as having a stable noise context, and uses"
" annotations on boxes to allow users to declare and configure that intent. "
"Every box is a scope that owns a set of qubits, operations that act on those"
" qubits, and a list of annotations. Samplomatic annotations specify "
"*directives* and *dressings*. Directives specify what to do with the box, "
"for example, twirl the box. Dressings are groups of parameterized gates to "
"add to the left- or right-side of the box, for example, a layer of single "
"qubit gates. The gates in a dressing incorporate gates from the box and "
"operations required to enact directives, such as the following:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Gates in the box that are compatible with and are on the same side as the "
"parameterized gates.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Twirling gates sampled from a set to randomize the box.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Noise injection gates sampled from a Pauli Lindblad map.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "User-specified basis changing gates.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Note that directives can alter dressings of other boxes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example {#example}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose we want to twirl the following circuit, adding random Pauli gates "
"before and after the parallel entangling gates that don’t change the logical"
" content of the circuit, but that do change the effective noise model.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![../\\_images/undressed\\_pauli.drawio.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/undressed_pauli.drawio.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit to Pauli twirl.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is achieved by stratifying the circuit into boxes and adding twirl "
"annotations.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![../\\_images/dressed\\_pauli\\_twirl.drawio.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/dressed_pauli_twirl.drawio.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Circuit with Pauli twirling directives. The `@` symbol is used to specify "
"directives, dressing by default is on the left.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each dressed box contains a layer of single-qubit gates and a layer of two-"
"qubit entangling gates on disjoint pairs of qubits. The layer of entangling "
"gates is surrounded by layers of random Pauli gates in such a way that the "
"box’s logical action is unchanged. These random Pauli layers are *virtual* "
"in the same way as a virtual Z gate. They do not add operations to the "
"circuit, but instead act as a directive to alter how adjacent single-qubit "
"gates are implemented.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![../\\_images/pauli\\_twirl.drawio.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/pauli_twirl.drawio.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Circuit with dressings and gates from directives. Dressings are the dashed "
"boxes. Pauli layers attached by arrows cancel each other out. The final "
"Pauli layer will be applied as bit flips to the measurement outcomes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The random Pauli layer between the entangling gates and single-qubit gates "
"is composed into the layer of single-qubit gates and is implemented in its "
"dressing. The other random Pauli layer will be composed into the dressing of"
" the next dressed box.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To summarize, the left (or right) twirl directive implements a random Pauli "
"in this box’s dressing and applies the Pauli that undoes it in the next (or "
"previous) box’s dressing. The inject noise and basis change directives are "
"analogous.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Circuit randomization with virtual gates {#circuit-randomization-with-"
"virtual-gates}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Samplomatic uses the framework of *virtual gates* to reason about circuits "
"with dressed boxes. Conceptually, and as implemented in a "
"[`Samplex`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-"
"samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex\") "
"instance produced by the `build()` process, virtual gates are generated at "
"the boundary of the box opposite its dressing. These virtual gates are moved"
" through the circuit in a prescribed way and need to be composed into a "
"dressing. If all virtual gates can be composed into a dressing, "
"randomizations of the circuit can be built procedurally.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![../\\_images/dressed\\_box.drawio.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/dressed_box.drawio.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit with twirl, basis change, and inject noise directives.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Gates on the side of the dressing that are compatible with the dressing’s "
"template parametrization can be composed into it, reducing the number of "
"physical gates. These are called *easy* gates. The remainder of the box is "
"called *hard* and is implemented as is.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![../\\_images/dressed\\_box\\_uncollected.drawio.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/dressed_box_uncollected.drawio.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Examples of circuits with hanging virtual gates. The virtual gates on the "
"opposite side of the dressing have nowhere to be implemented.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![../\\_images/dressed\\_box\\_collected.drawio.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/dressed_box_collected.drawio.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Examples of circuits where all virtual gates are composed into dressings. "
"Measurements have Pauli gates composed in by accounting for the bitflip they"
" induce.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![../\\_images/dressed\\_box\\_mixed\\_collect.drawio.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/dressed_box_mixed_collect.drawio.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Complex example where all virtual gates are collected. Virtual gates "
"generated by one box can be composed into different dressings.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This allows for constructions where dressed boxes do not need to have the "
"same width.\n"
msgstr ""
